From a1af059a4eb2680cc6900092303ec661a4c3d568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jarren Rocks <8302364+jarrenrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 19:02:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/54] Eight new worlds, water, wildlife, drones, ambient
 audio, and an Animal Crossing look
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Eleven planets instead of three: Dune, Canopy, Shoreline, Archipelago, Frost, Cinder,
Harvest and Blossom join Luna, Mars and Terra. A planet preset now carries its water,
shore, weather, clouds, fauna, ambience and colour grade, and a named `shape` bends the
height field into an island, a coast or dunes; flooded craters are the lakes and lava.

Water is the colony's own: a MeshPhysicalMaterial with Gerstner swell, per-vertex depth
for turquoise shallows and foam bands, sun sparkle, and ripple rings anything can trigger.

Fauna: boid flocks, butterflies, leaping fish and cargo drones running crates between
the lander and active sites — instanced, vertex-animated, casting shadows.

Ambient audio on the Web Audio API: per-world beds that cross-fade, events on their own
clocks, and positional voices (hammering, the ship, drones, shorelines) attenuated by
distance from the camera. Every sound has a synthesised fallback; real samples override
by name through public/audio/manifest.json.

The look: a world-curve shader patch that bends the ground away toward the horizon,
cumulus on the sky dome, a colour grade pass with lifted shadows and a soft vignette.

Kenney's Nature Kit (CC0) is packed into nature.glb with vertex-baked colours for the
palms, cacti, pines and canopies the Forest pack does not have.

