Subject: [PATCH 05/54] Dig lake-world craters to the waterline, let clouds
 reach the horizon, lighten Cinder's night

Folding the far-field noise to keep lake worlds above water also lifted every crater floor
above it, so the lakes and the lava were puddles. Bowls on those worlds are now dug down to
the waterline rather than down from the ground. Clouds fade later toward the horizon and
cover more of the sheet; Cinder's night sun and ambient come up so the ground is not black.

