From 668b4b0f3920d1a13428e64ad25b04bb25b0b3e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jarren Rocks <8302364+jarrenrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 21:53:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/54] Cap the crew by who matters, and drop the cascade; real
 boids; denser scatter
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The roster cap subtracted the astronauts still walking home from itself, so shrinking it
sent a batch home, the batch ate the budget, and three polls later the whole colony was on
the ramp — and it cut by repo order, so the ones waiting on you went first. The cap now
keeps blocked, waiting and working threads first, and anything merely over the display
budget vanishes in place rather than walking home like an archive.

Birds are Reynolds boids over a local neighbourhood with a drifting wander instead of a
per-frame kick, a smoothed heading for the body and a bank taken from the lateral force;
the model is a scrap of body on two thin swept wings. Scatter budget goes from 900 to 2400
and leans toward the colony.

