From fc8e115e168f34217378c968e1e5c84204083b7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jarren Rocks <8302364+jarrenrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:32:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/54] Motes and fireflies on the things that matter, a Resume
 door for forgotten threads, and a sound test
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every building near the view sheds a slow mote of light — warm by day, its plot's accent
after dark — the lander's beacon draws a halo of its own, and living worlds fill with
fireflies once the sun is down. Weather is spawned around the camera; these are spawned on
places, which is what makes a place feel inhabited.

An old thread the desktop app has dropped from its list cannot be navigated to, and Open
quietly does nothing. Dormant threads get a second button that asks the harness to re-import
the CLI transcript instead, at the cost of a new untitled session.

Settings gains a Sound test: every bed and event of the current world, the positional loops
and cues, then everything else, each with a play button and whether it is a recording or a
synth. Beds fade in for eight seconds and out again; the next button replaces the last.

