From 9e09fc499e20f52c68dcc549ff2e769d665a0a52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jarren Rocks <8302364+jarrenrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:46:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/54] Badges drawn after bloom, crates that actually drop,
 six selection phrases, and Aerie

Badges and name plates move to an overlay layer drawn by their own pass once bloom has
been added, so the one ? that wants you is a crisp symbol rather than a smear. Drones now
let their crate go: it falls, bounces on the deck, skids and fades. Clicking an astronaut
gets one of six little robot phrases from where it stands. A sleeper sent home stands up
and walks instead of sitting back down. Flocks no longer restart on a quality change.

Resume is gone; Cursor threads open the repo in Cursor and say so, and the card names the
harness. Aerie is a floating island in the sky: past its rim the ground falls out of sight,
ready for the underside, vines and cloud sea being built for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
