From dd69b5cafe6d3110075350c79321259dcd796320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jarren Rocks <8302364+jarrenrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:55:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/54] A meadow of wispy grass on the living worlds

One InstancedMesh of tens of thousands of tapered blades, planted in tufts clear of the
plots and the ship, swaying to a wind that travels across the field, coloured root to tip
from the planet's own ground. Terra, Shoreline, Archipelago, Canopy, Harvest, Blossom and
Aerie have it; the airless and the dead worlds do not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
