From: Jarren Rocks <8302364+jarrenrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:21:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/54] Aerie: the island is the colony's own hex footprint

One jagged rock plug per hex cell, merged into a single mass, with stalactites
rooted under the soil and the big ones under the middle of the island. The
plugs reach out under the grass margin so the ground has a soil lip instead
of a paper edge, and the terrain shader frays that edge with noise rather than
cutting it in arcs. Vines hang from the edges that face open sky. The rock is
rebuilt whenever the plots change, so the island grows and shrinks with the
colony.

