From b3419a93419ba87f08981c6b72554423536c0ffd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri <dimitri@moving-in.nl>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:55:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/54] Front the attached terminal window instead of importing
 into the desktop app

A terminal-started thread that is still running already has a window on
this machine. Opening it used to fall through to claude://resume, which
imports the transcript into the Claude desktop app as a second, untitled
session. Now the adapter hands the live CLI pid along, and on Windows the
server walks the process's parent chain to the first windowed ancestor
(Windows Terminal, an IDE) and fronts that window instead. Threads the
desktop app owns keep using the deep link, which navigates to the tab the
app already has; when no window can be found the URL runs as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
