From 2da3b2428c66faa70c7257d362364f4fb3672179 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri <dimitri@moving-in.nl>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 13:20:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/54] Shared colonies: visit a teammate's colony read-only
 over the LAN
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two Bot Crossing installs on one intranet can now share. Sharing is off by
default; when its owner turns it on, a machine answers a read-only guest API
and announces itself over UDP, and a visitor's map folds the neighbour's
repos in as their own named district beside the home zones.

Server:
- guest.mjs: a second HTTP listener (0.0.0.0:5275) with exactly /guest/info
  and /guest/threads. Read-only is structural — the action routes do not
  exist on the socket, and thread refs / transcript paths are stripped
  before anything leaves.
- discovery.mjs: a UDP heartbeat (5276) — announce while sharing, always
  listen; peers expire after three missed beats, own echo ignored by id.
- neighbors.mjs: fetch each configured neighbour's guest API on a 2s timeout
  and merge the *cached* answer, so a slow or sleeping peer never delays the
  owner's own map. Guest threads are tagged (guest:<host>:<id>, colony name)
  so two machines that both know a repo called 'wra' can never collide.
- api.mjs / serve.mjs / vite.config.js: a network block in colony.json
  (share, colonyName, neighbors) drives it all; /api/threads folds neighbours
  in, /api/neighbors backs the settings UI.

Client:
- plots.js: a colony anchors its district to a fixed outer ring by name, so a
  neighbour's repos cluster together and read as a separate settlement; a
  bolder floating banner names it.
- colony.js: guest plots carry their colony, cluster at the anchor, dim when
  the colony goes offline, keep their ground when it returns.
- hud.js / main.js: a Network settings section (share toggle, colony name,
  discovered + manual neighbours with online dots); visiting threads and
  districts are read-only in the UI, and every action guards server-side too.
- merge-state.js: network config merges local-wins like settings.

Tested: 43 unit tests pass (guest allowlist, merge tagging/collision safety,
discovery parsing, anchored district layout, network merge). A two-instance
end-to-end on one machine confirms a neighbour's district renders read-only,
actions are refused, and unplugging her dims the district.

