Subject: [PATCH 27/54] Per-session sharing: opt-in allowlist instead of
 sharing everything
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sharing no longer exposes every session. The guest API now serves only what
its owner opted in — an allowlist in network.shared holding session ids and
repo names — so an empty list shares nothing even with sharing on, and a
session is never exposed until it is named.

- server/api.mjs: the guest getThreads filters the scan to the allowlist
  (by thread id or by repo name) before anything leaves; network.shared is
  cleaned and carried in colony.json.
- Share controls where the actions already live: a 'Share with others' /
  'Stop sharing' button beside 'Hide from colony' toggles a whole repo
  (present and future sessions); a 'Share' / 'Stop sharing' button on the
  thread card toggles one session. A shared repo locks its sessions' own
  switch to 'Shared (repo)'. Shared rows carry a broadcast mark; Settings ->
  Shared colonies shows how many sessions are actually exposed.
- An active share button lights up teal and reads 'Stop sharing'.

