From 64de34b28d5528cb05444245a6535c964c005549 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri <dimitri@moving-in.nl>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 15:22:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 28/54] Guest listener: answer only added neighbours, not the
 whole LAN
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chantal's review (docs/claude/) flagged that server/guest.mjs bound 0.0.0.0
with no origin check, so anything on the allowlist was readable by any host
on the LAN that could reach the port. Now the listener answers only loopback
and the hosts the owner has added as neighbours — sharing is readable by the
colleagues you chose, not the whole network. Visiting becomes mutual: to be
visited, add the visitor.

- server/guest.mjs: hostAllowed(remoteAddr, allowedHosts) — loopback always,
  otherwise the neighbour hosts; strips the ::ffff: v4-mapping prefix. A
  refused host gets 403 before the allowlist is even consulted.
- server/api.mjs: passes the configured neighbours' hosts as the allowlist.
- install/README.md: warn not to run the installer over an existing clone
  (also from Chantal's review) — git pull instead.
- Tests: hostAllowed covers loopback spellings, v4-mapping, and a stranger
  on the same LAN being refused. 44 pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../2026-09-09-shared-colonies-design.md      | 18 ++++++++-
 install/README.md                             |  5 +++
 server/api.mjs                                |  3 ++
 server/guest.mjs                              | 38 ++++++++++++++++++-
 test/shared-colonies.test.mjs                 | 22 ++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 82 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

