From: Dimitri <dimitri@moving-in.nl>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 17:28:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/54] Self-heal a guest listener that only looks alive after
 sleep
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The reconcile tick restarted a *dropped* listener, but after the machine
sleeps a socket can keep server.listening === true while nothing actually
reaches it — so the heal was skipped and the owner still had to toggle
sharing to be seen again. Reconcile now probes the guest port with a real
1s TCP connect and force-restarts (GuestServer.restart) when nothing answers,
which is the honest check server.listening cannot give.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
