From e1359b8bad369e2a438252c9335b37908d54207c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri <dimitri@moving-in.nl>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:30:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 32/54] Make sharing work over a VPN: open firewall to all
 profiles, surface refused IPs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two changes so a VPN (FortiClient among them) can carry a visit once the VPN
routes client-to-client:

- Firewall opens on profile=any, not just private, since a VPN adapter is
  often classified public/domain. Safe because the guest listener already
  answers only added neighbours (app-level origin check), so an open port is
  not open access. Installer + README updated.
- A NAT'ing VPN can present a different source IP than the one a colleague
  added, so they stay refused with no clue why. The guest server now remembers
  recently-refused stranger IPs (bounded, 5-min window) and the settings panel
  lists them under 'Tried to visit you' with a one-click Add — so the real
  address is a click away. Exposed via /api/neighbors.

README gains a VPN section (find your IP, ping test, the client-to-client
caveat). 46 tests pass.

