From 259f4349a53d0649530f09c90cc417fbb9592b4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jarren Rocks <8302364+jarrenrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:30:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 34/54] Phone in the left hand, hammer from the shoulder, crew
 held out of walls, drones spread out
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The check now raises the left arm — KayKit's idle with the arm turned up,
found by a coordinate search over the joints — holds the folding phone in
the hand with a phone-style screen of scrolling cards and a progress bar,
and lowers it again. Clips are tweaked at bake time through TWEAKS in
crew.js (per-bone scale, offset, ramp), with a dev rebake hook. The
hammering has its swing moved from the wrist to the shoulder.

Buildings, clutter and scatter carry a keep radius the crew is pushed out
of and put back on after every step, bucketed on a coarse grid; an astronaut
getting nowhere for a moment stops shuffling and picks another spot. Drones
claim sites, drop at a random spot on the roof, and hold their distance
from each other in the air.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
