From b15c61d559877175a7f5f8d245807c332fc7d4b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jarren Rocks <8302364+jarrenrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:49:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 36/54] Phone gripped by its bottom corner; no more running on
 the spot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The fist now holds the bottom corner of the phone instead of sitting on
the screen. A step the keep-out undid counts as a refused step, goals are
kept out of keep circles, the walk-round-the-circle never steps through a
blocked cell, and a settling astronaut's corrections stay out of its speed
— so a sleeper shoved about in a pocket sits rather than jogs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
