From 95f840b2a73af4dd8fd7a04b68cc789f018550c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jarren Rocks <8302364+jarrenrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 14:14:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 39/54] Crew that cannot get stuck, and a first load that walks
 out of the ship
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Routes are planned on a grid rasterised with a small travel radius, and
a search that fails goes to the closest point reached instead of nowhere.
Keep-out applies to standing astronauts only; walkers collide with the
grid, separation pushes them sideways at most, and one that gets nowhere
for most of a second ghosts through the crowd and re-routes. A wobble
check relocates anything jittering in place to clear, uncrowded ground.
Sleepers nudge rather than shove; a walk creeping its last metre counts as
arrived; a stuck astronaut no longer re-walks to the same site every poll.

On a first load the whole crew queues inside the ship and comes out of the
airlock one at a time, walking down the ramp — the ones waiting on you
first — instead of being found already standing everywhere. The door is
read after the ship's matrix is updated, which is why it used to be at
the world origin on the very first roster.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 README.md                |  35 ++++--
 src/agents/astronauts.js | 262 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/agents/navigation.js |  54 +++++++-
