From a00e724d831464074c0ea171e16fddfa4df35b22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Kohnstamm <kohnsts@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 07:50:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 40/54] Spawn the crew by status, not scan position, so the
 chips stay clickable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The HUD counts every thread but maxAgents caps the crew, and the cut was
positional — project size then thread age. A working thread is by
definition recently active, so it sorted last and was cut first: the
colony would say "1 building" with no builder on the surface to click.

capRoster (new, pure, node-testable like merge-state.js) cuts by status
priority instead, keeps incoming order within a status so a quiet scan
moves nobody, and guarantees every counted status one representative
even when a single loud status could fill the whole cap. Clicking a chip
whose astronauts were still capped out now opens the project card, which
lists every thread, instead of dead-ending on a hint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
