From 12245b65135616d748c0e671a9b2dfebc2bce9ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Kohnstamm <kohnsts@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:17:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 42/54] Address review: chip-only guarantees, leaver revival,
 cycling fallback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The representative guarantee now spends bodies only on statuses the HUD
makes clickable — seating a dormant astronaut by evicting a blocked one
bought nothing a chip can reach. A leaver whose thread re-enters the
roster is revived in place instead of despawning mid-walk (it had no
status edge to un-leave it), and no slot is reserved for it. The chip
fallback now groups project-less threads under 'unknown' like the
colony does, skips leavers, and cycles projects on repeat presses via
the same cursor as the astronaut path. Status ranking has one source
(statusRank in roster.js) instead of two that disagreed on unknowns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
