Half the crew stays human; the rest step off the ship as one of three
species, all carved out of the same id hash that already picks the suit
tone. A species is only a skin tint through the existing instance-colour
path, a stature folded into the root scale, and a four-row block of the
face atlas — the sixteen expressions are drawn per eye layout rather than
hand-drawn per species, so the human rows stay bit-identical and the
meshes, materials and draw calls are untouched.

The picker's head height and the badge clearance follow the stature, so
tall and short astronauts stay clickable where you aim.

