From 5edf624dc9061967523af42a157a8420b2730836 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Kohnstamm <kohnsts@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:43:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 47/54] A desert kit of its own: Karak builds in adobe instead
 of tinted hulls
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tools/build-desert-kit.mjs packs Kenney's Space Kit and a slice of Quaternius'
Ultimate Space Kit (both CC0) into desertbase.glb in the house convention —
one scene of named nodes, one material, one generated 8x4 gradient atlas.
Every triangle is classified into six desert swatches (Kenney by material
name, Quaternius by palette sample) and its UVs rewritten to the cell centre,
so the per-cell accent, night-glow and PBR machinery works on it unchanged.

Buildings now carry a kit: per-kit surface/accent/tint tables and a per-kit
catalogue in buildings.js, ten desert recipes, and the launch pad kept rare.
The planet picks the architecture (planet.buildingKit), and a planet switch
that crosses a kit boundary rebuilds the colony's buildings — a kit is baked
into geometry, unlike the tint, which the desert kit drops entirely.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
