From c61e922f8042ee9ee47d3989bd940845b85c658f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Austin <76120216+zachaustin01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:24:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 49/54] Add an MCP factory building with glowing call pipes

Behind a new (off-by-default) settings toggle: a fixed building housing
the MCP servers an agent calls into, one glowing socket per server. A
tube arcs from an astronaut to its server's socket and pulses while the
thread is mid-call, fading out rather than snapping off when it ends.

Claude Code's harness adapter now reports which MCP server a running
thread is calling (mcp__<server>__<tool>) as thread.activeMcp; Codex
and Cursor have no per-tool-call visibility yet, so their threads just
report none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
