From 0a462c673786e85ec4ef333f24d75bc20c869a23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "dojacatbrightfire[bot]"
 <296164176+dojacatbrightfire[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:26:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 54/54] feat(openclaw): wire subagent visualization and MCP
 factory pipes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The transcripts carry no parent-child metadata, but the gateway's own
session registry does: a spawned sub-agent's entry names the session
that started it under spawnedBy, and that key's entry names the session
our thread ids are built from. A spawn that moved in the last five
minutes becomes one of its parent thread's subagents — the small
astronauts the colony orbits around the parent — resolved per agent
registry, read once per changed mtime like every other cached fact.

checkRunning now also says what a run is inside of: a last transcript
record that is a tool call names the tool in flight, reported as
activeMcp while running and cleared the moment its result lands.
OpenClaw flattens MCP tools to <server>__<tool>, so the server is what
the factory's socket is named for; a built-in tool stands in as its own
name. The growing-file case reads the tail too — growth alone is not
the story, since a file can swell with the toolResult of a call that
just finished.
---
 server/harnesses/openclaw.mjs | 200 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 176 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/server/harnesses/openclaw.mjs b/server/harnesses/openclaw.mjs
index f439fab..e490394 100644
--- a/server/harnesses/openclaw.mjs
+++ b/server/harnesses/openclaw.mjs
@@ -18,6 +18,12 @@
  * voted out of the paths, GitHub refs and command lines the transcript mentions — see
  * `detectProject`.
  *
+ * Two facts the transcripts alone cannot say come from beside them. The gateway keeps a
